    "final_text": "The todo CLI is built, and all 12 tests pass (`npm test`, which runs `node --test`).\n\n- **Commands:** `add`, `list`, `complete <id>` and `delete <id>` work as you specified, and todos are stored in `todos.json` in the current directory. Each todo has `id`, `text`, `completed` and `createdAt`.\n- **List output:** each line looks like `1 [x] text`, and an empty list prints \"No todos found.\"\n- **Edge cases:** a missing or blank text, a missing id, a non-numeric or negative id, an id that doesn't exist, and an unknown or missing command all print an error and exit with code 1.\n- **Corrupt file:** a `todos.json` that isn't valid JSON is treated as an empty list, and the next write overwrites it.\n- **Ids:** a new id is the highest existing id plus 1. If you delete the highest-numbered todo, its id is reused by the next add.\n- **Tests:** they run the real CLI in a temporary directory and cover every command and the edge cases above.\n\nThe code is in `index.js` and the tests are in `test.js`, with a `package.json` alongside. I haven't committed anything.",
